{"id": "EUVD-2026-80633", "enisaUuid": "8c80ae74-128d-3226-8a4d-ba109196233b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: typec: ucsi: displayport: Fix OOB altmode array index\n\nThe UCSI displayport driver indexes the connector's port altmode array\nwith the GET_CURRENT_CAM response after checking it is not 0xff. The\nport altmode array is UCSI_MAX_ALTMODES elements long. If the PPM\nreturns an invalid GET_CURRENT_CAM response above UCSI_MAX_ALTMODES and\nnot equal to 0xff, the kernel may crash with an array index OOB error.\n\nUpdate the UCSI displayport driver to verify the current cam is less\nthan UCSI_MAX_ALTMODES before accessing the port altmode array.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:33:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:56:39", "baseScore": 7.7, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8fde7e4a366184e9a6aa95541e52933a73c00a74", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/83f1abd62cc134700ba92e1e2dc650a49a185497", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ffed96ef986e2cdf986aa4a4506a5e6dcdf4456", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/58e0ee293ec5e06cacbe3953ad44042f1473dae9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac9f878c468052af6571e8639ab1c3ae040b908f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/33a81acd2d1d0667d4eff93cb90339fa53e617e8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bdaaf3074aedce8f1b173cc363d61cff5f6a585f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/04cec690b1fd9d1c4c314b91a10d8c68a3acfe18"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hg73-43cm-xh29", "CVE-2026-90025"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02f8e6dd-4d9b-3dfb-8287-51624f933eff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "2a49d573-7218-3ca2-82dc-2b1bbd21fe53", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "af8622f6a585d8d82b11cd7987e082861fd0edd3 <ac9f878c468052af6571e8639ab1c3ae040b908f"}, {"